 "amendments": {
  "items": {
   "": {
    "actClause": "AN ACT to amend the insurance law, in relation to requiring certain health and casualty insurers to provide coverage for prenatal vitamins",
    "basePrintNo": "S6309",
    "basePrintNoStr": "S6309-2009",
    "coSponsors": {
     "items": [],
     "size": 0
    },
    "fullText": "",
    "fullTextFormats": [],
    "fullTextHtml": "",
    "fullTextTemplate": "",
    "lawCode": "Amd §§3216, 3221 & 4303, Ins L",
    "lawSection": "Insurance Law",
    "memo": " BILL NUMBER:  S6309\n\n TITLE OF BILL :\nAn act to amend the insurance law, in relation to requiring certain\nhealth and casualty insurers to provide coverage for prenatal vitamins\n\n\n PURPOSE :\nTo require certain insurers to provide coverage for prenatal vitamins.\n\n SUMMARY OF PROVISIONS :\nSection 1. Describes which individual medical policies must provide\ncoverage for prenatal maternity care which includes prenatal vitamins.\nCoverage of the prenatal vitamins are subject to annual deductibles\nand coinsurance that are consistent with those established for a given\npolicy.\n\nSection 2. Describes which group or blanket medical policies must\nprovide coverage for prenatal maternity care which includes prenatal\nvitamins.  Coverage of the prenatal vitamins are subject to annual\ndeductibles and coinsurance that are consistent with those established\nfor a given policy.\n\nSection 3. States that every contract issued by a corporation which\nprovides hospital service, medical expense indemnity or both shall\nprovide coverage for prenatal maternity care which includes prenatal\nvitamins. Coverage will be made available at the inception of all new\ncontracts and at any anniversary date subject to evidence of\ninsurability for all other contracts.  This coverage will be subject\nto deductibles and coinsurance as deemed appropriate by the\nsuperintendent.\n\nSection 4. Effective date.\n\n JUSTIFICATION :\nPrenatal vitamins are vitamin supplements taken before and during\npregnancy with the intention of providing women with nutrients that\nhelp towards a healthy pregnancy. This legislation would ensure women\nacross New York State have access to quality prenatal vitamins without\nhaving to shoulder a massive financial burden. Prenatal maternity care\nis a vital healthcare service that needs to provided to people of all\nsocioeconomic backgrounds.\n\n LEGISLATIVE HISTORY :\nNew Bill.\n\n FISCAL IMPLICATIONS :\nTo be determined.\n\n EFFECTIVE DATE :\nThis act shall take effect immediately.\n",
